.nh
.TH "PB-ENV-HOST" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-env-host - Manage encrypted host ENV projections


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb env host [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage encrypted host ENV projections

.PP
Provision an exact selection of encrypted ENV values to an enrolled host. The selection must be explicit and can be emptied deliberately.

.PP
ENV values are encrypted before they leave the client. Commands select personal, team, or host scope explicitly; list output shows metadata rather than secret values. Unlock the local vault when a key operation requires it.

.PP
With --json, this command group lists its available commands.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for host


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-env(1)\fP, \fBpb-env-host-provision(1)\fP
